      "writtenOn": "2025-02-17T10:04:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Updated the comment.\n\nI fully agree that adding an internal prefix to names could also work.\n\nThis addresses both fields and methods. Consider the below example. `B` is kept, but nothing is keeping `A` or `A.f`. Therefore, normally R8 would change `A.f` from being private to being public, which means that `f` now becomes part of the public API surface of the library via `B`.\n\nWhen `Protect_api_surface` is enabled, `A.f` won\u0027t be made public when `B` is kept.\n\n```\nclass A {\n  private int f;\n}\n\npublic class B extends A {}\n\n-keep public class * {\n  public protected \u003cfields\u003e;\n  public protected \u003cmethods\u003e;\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "aac5253c_9c77acc1",
      "range": {
